('An antiparticle has the same mass and opposite electric charge to its particle. The positron is the electron antiparticle: both have mass $m_e$, but their charges are $+e$ and $-e$.','How does an antiparticle compare with its particle?','What is the antiparticle of an electron?'),
('β− decay emits an electron and an electron antineutrino; β+ decay emits a positron and an electron neutrino.','Which neutral particle accompanies β− decay?','Which neutral particle accompanies β+ decay?'),
